  topicId: wildlife
  title: Homes for wildlife
  body: Old forests shelter wildlife such as the Philippine Eagle, which needs large
    stands of forest in Mindanao and the Sierra Madre. Losing that forest takes away
    the animals' home and releases its stored carbon, and newly planted trees take
    decades to replace either.
